{"authored" [{"question" "q-346051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{6}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-7,$ calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)-1)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)-1)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{6}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,{\\int }_{1}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(7)\\,-\\,x\\,{|}_{1}^{6} \\\\  & =14\\,-\\,(6-1) \\\\  & =14\\,-\\,5 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-2$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3,$ then what is ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+3 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 1 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+2\\cdot x\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =1+2(3-0) \\\\  & =1+6 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $f$ and $g$ be continuous functions such that ${\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=9,\\,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4,$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=10.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-4 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the adjacent intervals rule and substituting known values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the sum rule for definite integrals,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(9)+(-8) \\\\  & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =19-{\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =19-10 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "e08a60b4d97f3d47007b4efdb7f7fd606625bb3eb2098cf82658b868fe3b7300" "basis" 1106 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{7}^{2}(-5)\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=15$ and ${\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7f4b6d986a204ede4176d10fe6c7622efc06d1bb51e9d82bd332165cb1faab" "basis" 1550 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{7}^{2}(-5)\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ (-5){\\int }_{7}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ 5{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+3 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7f4b6d986a204ede4176d10fe6c7622efc06d1bb51e9d82bd332165cb1faab" "basis" 1550 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec074b36716a9ea8e20e6a66e2b639608de20588b4549d3a1bb063ca4f95a325" "basis" 1550 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7f4b6d986a204ede4176d10fe6c7622efc06d1bb51e9d82bd332165cb1faab" "basis" 1550 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7f4b6d986a204ede4176d10fe6c7622efc06d1bb51e9d82bd332165cb1faab" "basis" 1550 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042484/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-73339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{5}^{3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-5$, calculate\n${\\int }_{3}^{5}(5-4f(x))\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-73339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{5}^{3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factoring out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{5}(5-4f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\cdot x{|}_{3}^{5}-4(5) \\\\  & =5(5-3)-20 \\\\  & =10-20 \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-73339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b24daaccb5fb7e819d16cecc3a39057b5456b8b66229fc259eacaaa4703dffa3"} {"question" "q-73339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-73339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-15"] ["math" "-20"] ["math" "-25"] ["math" "-30"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-73339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-2$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3,$ then what is ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+3 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 1 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+2\\cdot x\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =1+2(3-0) \\\\  & =1+6 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b24daaccb5fb7e819d16cecc3a39057b5456b8b66229fc259eacaaa4703dffa3"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{6}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-7,$ calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)-1)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)-1)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{6}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,{\\int }_{1}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(7)\\,-\\,x\\,{|}_{1}^{6} \\\\  & =14\\,-\\,(6-1) \\\\  & =14\\,-\\,5 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b24daaccb5fb7e819d16cecc3a39057b5456b8b66229fc259eacaaa4703dffa3"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{7}^{2}(-5)\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=15$ and ${\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{7}^{2}(-5)\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ (-5){\\int }_{7}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ 5{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+3 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b24daaccb5fb7e819d16cecc3a39057b5456b8b66229fc259eacaaa4703dffa3"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346213" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $f$ and $g$ be continuous functions such that ${\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=9,\\,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4,$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=10.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-4 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the adjacent intervals rule and substituting known values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the sum rule for definite integrals,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(9)+(-8) \\\\  & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =19-{\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =19-10 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b24daaccb5fb7e819d16cecc3a39057b5456b8b66229fc259eacaaa4703dffa3"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071004/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4a963e540c5a4b3eb5d12656126d96d99688dc07db2ca895531ba8b59426268"}] "usage" {"q-346225" [] "q-346051" [] "q-114133" [] "q-346213" []} "basis" 2530 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186287211 17592186287212 17592186287213 17592186287214 17592186287215 17592186287242 17592186287243 17592186287257 17592186315680] "immutable_fields" [[17592186287210 :answer-field/correct] [17592186287210 :answer-field/id] [17592186287210 :answer-field/key] [17592186287210 :answer-field/type] [17592186287241 :answer-field/correct] [17592186287241 :answer-field/id] [17592186287241 :answer-field/key] [17592186287241 :answer-field/type] [17592186287256 :answer-field/correct] [17592186287256 :answer-field/id] [17592186287256 :answer-field/key] [175